{"timestamp": "2026-02-04 19:49:12.566711", "event": "llm_start", "messages": "content='Based on the diagnosis report: ### Troubleshooting Diagnosis Report\\n\\n#### Network Description\\nThe network is an SDN star topology with one central switch (switch_0) and multiple edge switches (switch_1, switch_2, switch_3, switch_4). Hosts (host_1, host_2, host_3, host_4) are connected to edge switches, and all devices share a single access subnet (10.0.0.0/24). The SDN controller operates at 20.0.0.100 and manages the switches via OpenFlow.\\n\\n#### Observations\\n1. **Host Reachability Results**:\\n   - The reachability test between hosts indicates an anomaly. All tests between hosts (e.g., host_1 to host_4, host_2 to host_3, etc.) returned a status of \"unknown.\"\\n   - No data was transmitted (`tx`), received (`rx`), or measured for packet loss, round-trip time (RTT), or other metrics.\\n\\n2. **Implications**:\\n   - The inability to determine reachability between hosts suggests a potential issue in the network\\'s forwarding plane or control plane.\\n   - The SDN controller may not be properly programming flow rules on the switches, or there could be a connectivity issue between the controller and the switches.\\n\\n#### Next Steps\\nTo further diagnose the root cause, the following areas need investigation:\\n1. **SDN Controller Connectivity**:\\n   - Verify if the switches are successfully connected to the SDN controller at 20.0.0.100:6633.\\n\\n2. **Switch Configuration**:\\n   - Check the OpenFlow configuration and flow rules on all switches (switch_0, switch_1, switch_2, switch_3, switch_4).\\n\\n3. **Host-Switch Connectivity**:\\n   - Confirm that hosts are properly connected to their respective edge switches and that the edge switches are forwarding traffic to the central switch.\\n\\n4. **Central Switch Functionality**:\\n   - Ensure that switch_0 is correctly forwarding traffic between edge switches.\\n\\n5. **Network Interface and Routing**:\\n   - Validate the network interfaces and routing configurations on all devices.\\n\\n#### Conclusion\\nThe network is experiencing abnormal behavior, as hosts are unable to communicate with each other. This issue is likely related to the SDN controller or switch configurations. Further investigation is required to pinpoint the root cause., please provide the submission. Do not submit if no report available.' additional_kwargs={} response_metadata={} id='60b6e033-0431-414a-aa40-e19440bcdb8d'", "model": {"lc": 1, "type": "constructor", "id": ["langchain", "chat_models", "openai", "ChatOpenAI"], "kwargs": {"model_name": "kt-gpt-oss-rh014", "temperature": 0.0, "openai_api_key": {"lc": 1, "type": "secret", "id": ["OPENAI_API_KEY"]}, "openai_api_base": "https://dev.kora.kt.co.kr/v2", "request_timeout": 180.0, "max_retries": 2}, "name": "ChatOpenAI"}}
